<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The key is <strong>balancing opt=
imization effort with actual impact</strong>. I don't memoize everything - =
that can actually hurt performance. Instead, I profile first, identify bott=
lenecks, then apply targeted optimizations.</p>
<hr>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Part 2: Deep Tec=
hnical Discussion (35 minutes)</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
cellent approach to render optimization. I can see you understand the nuanc=
es between helpful and harmful optimizations. Now, let's dive deeper into t=
he performance fundamentals. You mentioned Core Web Vitals earlier. At NAB,=
 we're particularly concerned with our LCP and CLS scores on our mortgage a=
pplication flow.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Can you walk me through your sys=
tematic approach to diagnosing and improving these metrics? I'm especially =
interested in how you handle the trade-offs between performance and user ex=
perience in complex forms.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: This=
 is exactly the type of challenge I love tackling. <strong>Mortgage applica=
tions are particularly tricky because they're conversion-critical and invol=
ve heavy forms with dynamic content</strong>. Let me walk through my system=
atic approach:</p>
