<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Results I've achieved wi=
th this approach:</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>LCP improved from 3.8s =
to 2.1s</strong> (45% improvement)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>CLS reduced from 0.25 t=
o 0.08</strong> (68% improvement)</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Form completion rate in=
creased by 34%</strong></li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>User frustration events=
 decreased by 56%</strong></li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The key insight is that <strong>=
performance optimization in financial applications isn't just about speed -=
 it's about building trust through reliability and smooth interactions</str=
ong>.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ou=
tstanding! I particularly appreciate how you tie performance metrics to bus=
iness outcomes. That's exactly the level of thinking we need here. Your app=
roach to progressive enhancement and predictive space allocation is very so=
phisticated.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Let me challenge you with a spec=
ific scenario we face: Our Internet Banking dashboard needs to display real=
-time account balances, transaction feeds, and market data for up to 15 dif=
ferent accounts simultaneously. Users often have multiple browser tabs open=
, and we're seeing performance degradation. How would you architect the dat=
a fetching and state management for this scenario?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: This=
 is a fascinating architectural challenge that really tests the boundaries =
of frontend performance. <strong>Real-time financial data with multiple acc=
ounts across tabs</strong> - that's exactly where naive implementations fal=
l apart. Let me outline my approach:</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Architecture Overview:</=
strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">The core principle is <strong>ce=
ntralized data management with intelligent subscription handling</strong>. =
I'd implement a hybrid approach using <strong>Shared Web Workers for cross-=
tab coordination</strong> and <strong>fine-grained reactive state managemen=
t</strong>.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1. Shared Web Worker for=
 Cross-Tab Data Management:</strong></p>
